    "terms": "REFERENCE SIMULATION — for internal acceptance testing only. This is an English operational paraphrase of the supplied Q1 screenshots, not a live promotion or approved legal terms. No real purchase, bank account, payment or entitlement is required or promised.\n\nEligibility: the reference campaign is for end consumers aged 18 or over purchasing for their own use. This simulation is limited to Germany, France, Italy, Spain and the Netherlands. Purchase an eligible new Graphics Card, Motherboard or Monitor directly from a retailer listed for the selected purchase country. Second-hand, refurbished, resale and returned products are not eligible. Retailers cannot submit claims for customers.\n\nReference qualifying period: 16–28 March 2026. Reference claim period: 30 March–26 April 2026, and at least 14 days after purchase. Exact stored timestamps reproduce the source's stated CET (UTC+01:00); the claim window overlaps daylight saving time and requires owner confirmation before any real launch. The active UAT copy may use different dates shown in its campaign settings.\n\nOne claim is allowed per participant and per household/address, with at most one product from each of the three categories. All products in a claim must appear on the same invoice. Cashback is the sum of the listed amounts for the selected products: up to EUR 30 for a graphics card, EUR 90 for a motherboard and EUR 60 for a monitor, giving a maximum EUR 180. There is no A+B bonus. The reference excludes combination with other promoter promotions; this simulation uses a named exclusivity group for related campaign copies.\n\nTo claim, provide participant and matching bank-account-holder details, invoice number and purchase date, the selected retailer, product model and serial number, a readable invoice and a photo of each selected product's serial-number label. The invoice should show the retailer, purchase date, product and purchase price. The source also requires AORUS membership and matching member email; verification remains manual in this simulation.\n\nThe source describes an acknowledgement email, an acceptance or denial response within 10 working days and bank transfer within 90 days after claim validation. UAT notifications and payments are simulated; working-day calendars and real email/bank integrations are not represented by this sample. Incomplete evidence may require additional information. Review and payment progress can be checked in the claim tracker. For a replacement, return, correction or missing confirmation, contact the campaign test owner through the configured support channel.\n\nThe EUR 100,000 budget, EUR 5,000 buffer, 1,000-claim limit and per-model quantity limit of 1 are sample operating settings, not values published in the screenshots. Availability and claim acceptance remain subject to the configured campaign controls. These terms must be replaced and reviewed before use for a real promotion.",
    "privacy": "UAT SIMULATION NOTICE. Use fictitious participant, invoice and bank details only. The reference campaign collected identity, contact, purchase, serial-number and bank details to administer cashback; marketing consent was optional. This sample does not reproduce the agency's controller/processor agreement or claim that its privacy notice applies to this system. The campaign owner must supply the approved privacy notice, retention policy and contact details before a real launch. The support address in this sample is deliberately non-deliverable.",
    "faq": "Q: Which products and countries can I test?\nA: The supplied Q1 product table contains 59 eligible models across Graphics Card, Motherboard and Monitor. This sample covers DE, FR, IT, ES and NL, using the same EUR cashback table.\n\nQ: Can I submit several products?\nA: Yes: at most one product per category, all on the same invoice, in one claim per participant and household. The maximum is EUR 180; there is no A+B bonus.\n\nQ: When can I apply?\nA: Wait at least 14 days after purchase and submit within the campaign's displayed claim window. The downloadable reference retains the historic Q1 dates; the separately seeded UAT activity may show shifted dates.\n\nQ: What evidence is needed?\nA: Upload a legible invoice showing the retailer, date, model and price, plus serial-number-label photos. Use synthetic evidence and fictitious bank details in UAT. The original requires AORUS membership with a matching email; membership is checked manually here.\n\nQ: Why can a claim still request information after I upload a file?\nA: Uploading evidence does not itself complete review. Check the review message and supply the requested information through the available claim workflow.\n\nQ: What are review and payment statuses?\nA: Review status records the eligibility decision; payment status records payout processing. Approval does not mean that a transfer has completed. Use the tracker for the current state.\n\nQ: How long does processing take?\nA: The source states 10 working days for an acceptance/denial response and 90 days from validation for payment. UAT uses simulated notifications and payment results; these are not real service or bank-transfer commitments.\n\nQ: What if my product was replaced or returned, or my details are incorrect?\nA: Contact the campaign test owner before proceeding. The reference excludes returned products and requires the bank account holder to match the claimant. The screenshot shows FAQ topics for replacements and corrections, but its collapsed answers are not available; no original answer is asserted here.\n\nQ: Can I select a retailer that is absent from the list?\nA: Choose an eligible retailer for the purchase country. An unlisted typed name does not create a participating retailer.",
